cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Topological Collapse and Asymmetric Divergence of Carmichael Pseudoprimes on the 6N Skeleton (Part XXXVI)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducer, data, figure, and paper for an empirical study of Carmichael
  numbers read through the 6N skeleton. Korselt's criterion forces a
  semipermeable membrane (left-wing Carmichael numbers are monochromatically
  6N-1) and a parity law, verified with zero violations over all 1547 Carmichael
  numbers up to 1e10; the right/left wing ratio R(X) diverges from 5.0 to 88.8
  across seven decades, with an unidentifiable asymptotic rate.
